# Cursor rules: FilsPay. Full rules: AGENTS.md (read it). Summary of what matters most:

# Verify, do not trust: comments, docs, ADRs, tests and AI answers are claims. Reproduce before you rely on them.

# Money: 1 BD = 1000 fils. Whole integer fils everywhere (BIGINT, never INTEGER, never float, never "cents").
# Parse text with parseBhdToFils ("4.75" -> 4750). Rates are basis points via applyRateFils (half to even).
# Splits use largest remainder so shares sum to the total. packages/money and the Go money package must match.

# Time: the settlement day is Asia/Bahrain midnight (UTC+3). Compute "today" in Bahrain, not from the UTC date.

# Ledger: ledger_entries is the truth; merchant_balances is a cache. Paid batches are final. Test merchants never settle.

# Security: crypto (not Math.random) for anything guessable. Scope every merchant query by the authenticated merchant.
# Enforce roles server-side. Impersonation is read-only. Verify signatures over raw bytes, fresh, constant-time.
# Lock the row before validating money operations; make them idempotent.

# Tests: evidence, not scripture. A test that asserts a bug (e.g. 4.75 -> 475) gets fixed with a comment saying why.
# New tests go in *.new.test.ts / *_test.go. Run scripts/ai/verify.sh (clean database per suite).
